No

31
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:41,000
No

32
00:01:41,000 --> 00:02:10,980
Thank you.

33
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:40,980
Thank you.

34
00:02:41,000 --> 00:02:43,000
Understudy?

35
00:02:43,000 --> 00:02:50,000
Excuse me, understudies are members who take the places of successors assigned to combat duty.

36
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:52,000
Or am I wrong in assuming that, Tsubasa-san?

37
00:02:52,000 --> 00:02:57,000
Yes, but in AKB's past, understudies were something different.

38
00:02:57,000 --> 00:03:03,000
In the event a successor couldn't appear in a concert, another member or trainee would take her place.

39
00:03:03,000 --> 00:03:06,000
That is what they used to call understudies.

40
00:03:06,000 --> 00:03:08,000
From the trainees?

41
00:03:08,000 --> 00:03:12,000
Concerts on planets with entertainment bands are dangerous.

42
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:18,000
Because of this, only those who had completed sufficient combat training could appear on stage.

43
00:03:18,000 --> 00:03:25,000
But with the current high demand for entertainment, we cannot maintain this policy.

44
00:03:25,000 --> 00:03:27,000
You want us to become understudies?

45
00:03:27,000 --> 00:03:30,000
We'll take over successors positions at concerts?

46
00:03:30,000 --> 00:03:33,000
I will now announce the members who will become understudies.

47
00:03:33,000 --> 00:03:39,000
Takamina's understudy will be Kanada Shinonomi.

48
00:03:39,000 --> 00:03:40,000
Yeah!

49
00:03:40,000 --> 00:03:43,000
Kojiharu's understudy will be Memori Kishida.

50
00:03:43,000 --> 00:03:44,000
Great!

51
00:03:44,000 --> 00:03:46,000
That's amazing, guys!

52
00:03:46,000 --> 00:03:49,000
Yukarin's understudy will be Megumi Wanaguchi.

53
00:03:49,000 --> 00:03:50,000
Yes!

54
00:03:50,000 --> 00:03:52,000
Oh my god, this is so great!

55
00:03:52,000 --> 00:03:59,000
Finally, Yuko's understudy will be Chiaris Solo.

56
00:03:59,000 --> 00:04:00,000
Yes!

57
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:01,000
Amazing!

58
00:04:01,000 --> 00:04:02,000
Uh-oh!

59
00:04:02,000 --> 00:04:06,000
You're getting tons of opportunities so quickly!

60
00:04:06,000 --> 00:04:08,000
That's great, Chiaris!

61
00:04:08,000 --> 00:04:10,000
Thank you.

62
00:04:10,000 --> 00:04:11,000
What's the meaning of this?

63
00:04:11,000 --> 00:04:15,000
If you're going in order, the 76th generation trainee should come first.

64
00:04:15,000 --> 00:04:16,000
That's not fair, Tsubasa-san.

65
00:04:16,000 --> 00:04:18,000
Why a 77th generation trainee?

66
00:04:18,000 --> 00:04:19,000
Yeah!

67
00:04:19,000 --> 00:04:20,000
What's that about?

68
00:04:20,000 --> 00:04:23,000
Just like Succession.

69
00:04:23,000 --> 00:04:28,000
The duration of a trainee's enrollment isn't a consideration when selecting understudies.

70
00:04:28,000 --> 00:04:33,000
Unlike Succession, we select understudies based not on the nature of their soul,

71
00:04:33,000 --> 00:04:35,000
but on their current abilities.

72
00:04:35,000 --> 00:04:38,000
If you're not satisfied with the results, practice.

73
00:04:38,000 --> 00:04:40,000
It's the only thing you can do.

74
00:04:42,000 --> 00:04:45,000
You're bringing back trainee understudies, huh?

75
00:04:45,000 --> 00:04:48,000
I'm not surprised the girls are agitated.

76
00:04:48,000 --> 00:04:51,000
Yesterday, Sensei-sensei...

77
00:04:52,000 --> 00:04:54,000
Understudies.

78
00:04:54,000 --> 00:04:55,000
Understudies.

79
00:04:55,000 --> 00:04:57,000
But Sensei, I don't...

80
00:04:57,000 --> 00:04:58,000
Understudies.

81
00:04:58,000 --> 00:05:07,000
Recently, I've noticed Sensei has been expressing wishes more actively than ever before.

82
00:05:07,000 --> 00:05:09,000
Besides, those lyrics...

83
00:05:09,000 --> 00:05:11,000
That one about the number of something?

84
00:05:11,000 --> 00:05:12,000
Yes.

85
00:05:12,000 --> 00:05:19,000
Ever since the 77th generation appeared, it's almost as though Sensei has been composing lyrics in response to them.

86
00:05:19,000 --> 00:05:21,000
Which means...

87
00:05:24,000 --> 00:05:29,000
Uh, trainees who weren't selected to be understudies have to practice on their own, huh?

88
00:05:29,000 --> 00:05:33,000
They told us we could take a break today, but what should we do?

89
00:05:33,000 --> 00:05:35,000
It's stingy of them, isn't it?

90
00:05:35,000 --> 00:05:39,000
I mean, they could've at least let us practice with them in a corner or something.

91
00:05:39,000 --> 00:05:40,000
Geez.

92
00:05:40,000 --> 00:05:41,000
There, there.

93
00:05:41,000 --> 00:05:42,000
Calm down, Yuka.

94
00:05:42,000 --> 00:05:45,000
In that case, let's binge on Snacks!

95
00:05:45,000 --> 00:05:47,000
I couldn't agree more!

96
00:05:47,000 --> 00:05:48,000
Huh?

97
00:05:48,000 --> 00:05:50,000
It's the 76th generation.

98
00:05:50,000 --> 00:05:55,000
It's kind of...

99
00:05:55,000 --> 00:05:57,000
Awful, I hate it!

100
00:05:57,000 --> 00:06:00,000
I hate impolite girls like that!

101
00:06:00,000 --> 00:06:02,000
Okay, let's enjoy our time off, you guys.

102
00:06:02,000 --> 00:06:05,000
Let's play, let's do karaoke, let's party!

103
00:06:05,000 --> 00:06:06,000
Alright!

104
00:06:06,000 --> 00:06:07,000
I want to do karaoke too!

105
00:06:07,000 --> 00:06:09,000
You'll go too, won't you?

106
00:06:09,000 --> 00:06:10,000
I don't think so.

107
00:06:10,000 --> 00:06:13,000
I'm going to rest at the dorm today.

108
00:06:13,000 --> 00:06:14,000
Yeah.

109
00:06:16,000 --> 00:06:19,000
Nagisa-san is a Yuko-san supporter.

110
00:06:19,000 --> 00:06:20,000
Yeah.

111
00:06:29,000 --> 00:06:30,000
This is different!

112
00:06:34,000 --> 00:06:35,000
From our regular lessons!

113
00:06:39,000 --> 00:06:41,000
This is a completely different level!

114
00:06:41,000 --> 00:06:53,000
No, that's not it!

115
00:06:53,000 --> 00:07:00,000
Right before you flows a river, its path is long and winding and it runs...

116
00:07:00,000 --> 00:07:01,000
Stop!

117
00:07:01,000 --> 00:07:06,000
You've got to show more emotion!

118
00:07:06,000 --> 00:07:09,000
Your audience won't get excited if you don't.

119
00:07:10,000 --> 00:07:20,000
When in your life you find a river, hold on until you fulfill all your dreams.

120
00:07:20,000 --> 00:07:23,000
Never lose sight of them, you can do it!

121
00:07:23,000 --> 00:07:24,000
You've passed!

122
00:07:24,000 --> 00:07:25,000
Really?

123
00:07:25,000 --> 00:07:26,000
Yeah!

124
00:07:26,000 --> 00:07:27,000
I'm glad you're my understudy.

125
00:07:27,000 --> 00:07:28,000
What?

126
00:07:28,000 --> 00:07:32,000
The original Takamina-san had more passion and leadership sense than anyone.

127
00:07:32,000 --> 00:07:33,000
You're the captain of the trainees too, aren't you?

128
00:07:33,000 --> 00:07:34,000
Takamina-san!

129
00:07:34,000 --> 00:07:35,000
Also, if you don't pull back on your dancing when you need to, you'll be off-tempo.

130
00:07:35,000 --> 00:07:36,000
Yeah!

131
00:07:36,000 --> 00:07:37,000
That's all for this afternoon.

132
00:07:37,000 --> 00:07:38,000
I'll work you hard again tonight!

133
00:07:38,000 --> 00:07:39,000
Got it!

134
00:07:39,000 --> 00:07:40,000
I'm so hungry!

135
00:07:40,000 --> 00:07:41,000
I wonder what's for lunch today?

136
00:07:41,000 --> 00:07:42,000
Chinchao Rosu?

137
00:07:42,000 --> 00:07:43,000
Chinchao Rosu?

138
00:07:45,000 --> 00:07:48,000
Thierry!

139
00:07:48,000 --> 00:07:49,000
We're finished!

140
00:07:49,000 --> 00:07:50,000
It's time for lunch!

141
00:07:50,000 --> 00:07:51,000
But...

142
00:07:51,000 --> 00:07:55,000
Thierry, you've got to bulk up or you're never going to make it through the setlist!

143
00:07:55,000 --> 00:07:57,000
You're going to have to eat lots more and strengthen yourselves!

144
00:07:57,000 --> 00:07:59,000
I think so, you've got to have to wait a minute!

145
00:07:59,000 --> 00:08:01,000
No, wait!

146
00:08:01,000 --> 00:08:03,000
No, no, no, no!

147
00:08:03,000 --> 00:08:04,000
No, no!

148
00:08:04,000 --> 00:08:05,000
No, no!

149
00:08:05,000 --> 00:08:07,000
No, no!

150
00:08:07,000 --> 00:08:08,000
No, no!

151
00:08:10,000 --> 00:08:11,000
No!

152
00:08:11,000 --> 00:08:12,120
Strengthen yourself!

153
00:08:12,860 --> 00:08:14,120
Uh, okay.

154
00:08:15,540 --> 00:08:16,580
Oh my gosh.

155
00:08:17,100 --> 00:08:19,160
There are so many bell peppers today.

156
00:08:19,580 --> 00:08:20,620
Thanks for the food.

157
00:08:24,000 --> 00:08:27,460
I must not be good enough to be an ender study yet.

158
00:08:28,180 --> 00:08:29,600
I'm so hungry.

159
00:08:30,400 --> 00:08:31,320
Welcome back.

160
00:08:31,560 --> 00:08:32,380
How was your lesson?

161
00:08:32,860 --> 00:08:34,620
It's even harder than I imagined.

162
00:08:35,140 --> 00:08:36,580
That sounds amazing.

163
00:08:37,740 --> 00:08:39,120
It's so intense.

164
00:08:39,120 --> 00:08:40,980
My hips are coming loose.

165
00:08:41,580 --> 00:08:43,260
Are you okay, Mamori-san?

166
00:08:45,880 --> 00:08:48,620
Chiri-chan, you don't like bell peppers, right?

167
00:08:49,260 --> 00:08:49,920
Uh, yes.

168
00:08:50,560 --> 00:08:52,080
I cut back on the peppers.

169
00:08:52,460 --> 00:08:53,120
Thank you.

170
00:08:53,580 --> 00:08:55,000
Thank you for the food!

171
00:08:55,640 --> 00:08:57,740
Chef Papa, the peppers were good!

172
00:08:57,880 --> 00:08:58,940
Thank you!

173
00:08:59,240 --> 00:08:59,600
Mmm!

174
00:08:59,900 --> 00:09:02,820
Uh, actually, could I get extra peppers, please?

175
00:09:02,940 --> 00:09:03,280
Oh?

176
00:09:03,620 --> 00:09:05,040
Are you challenging yourself?

177
00:09:06,140 --> 00:09:08,760
Here, I'll load it up with tons of peppers!

178
00:09:08,760 --> 00:09:08,900
I need one here!

179
00:09:11,000 --> 00:09:11,700
I need one here!

180
00:09:11,700 --> 00:09:12,300
Bow!

181
00:09:16,880 --> 00:09:17,220
Um!

182
00:09:20,000 --> 00:09:20,380
Hmm?

183
00:09:26,060 --> 00:09:26,540
Huh?

184
00:09:26,540 --> 00:09:29,540
Huh?

185
00:09:29,540 --> 00:09:31,540
Sexy!

186
00:09:31,540 --> 00:09:35,540
Alright, I'm in perfect form again today!

187
00:09:35,540 --> 00:09:37,540
I want you!

188
00:09:37,540 --> 00:09:39,540
I need you!

189
00:09:39,540 --> 00:09:41,540
I love you!

190
00:09:41,540 --> 00:09:43,540
Okay.

191
00:09:43,540 --> 00:09:45,540
Sexy!

192
00:09:49,540 --> 00:09:51,540
Jenny, what are you doing?

193
00:09:51,540 --> 00:09:54,540
It's not what it looks like.

194
00:09:54,540 --> 00:10:03,540
Sorry. You're working really hard to get closer to Yuko-san, aren't you?

195
00:10:03,540 --> 00:10:04,540
Yeah.

196
00:10:04,540 --> 00:10:07,540
It makes me kind of happy.

197
00:10:07,540 --> 00:10:09,540
Hey, listen.

198
00:10:09,540 --> 00:10:13,540
Congratulations on becoming… an understudy.

199
00:10:13,540 --> 00:10:15,540
I hadn't told you.

200
00:10:15,540 --> 00:10:18,540
Thank you.

201
00:10:18,540 --> 00:10:26,540
Hey, let's look at the Yuko-san notes I wrote until our evening lessons, weren't you?

202
00:10:26,540 --> 00:10:27,540
Yuko-san notes?

203
00:10:27,540 --> 00:10:28,540
Yeah.

204
00:10:28,540 --> 00:10:31,540
My Yuko-san summary notes.

205
00:10:31,540 --> 00:10:35,540
Chiri, isn't there some kind of big secret you're hiding from everyone?

206
00:10:35,540 --> 00:10:37,540
Anything you want to tell us?

207
00:10:37,540 --> 00:10:38,540
What?

208
00:10:38,540 --> 00:10:39,540
Don't play dumb with us.

209
00:10:39,540 --> 00:10:41,540
We just happened to find this.

210
00:10:41,540 --> 00:10:42,540
Ugh!

211
00:10:42,540 --> 00:10:46,540
Chiri, you're the daughter of the Zodiac Corporation CEO.

212
00:10:46,540 --> 00:10:48,540
On top of that…

213
00:10:48,540 --> 00:10:49,540
Ugh!

214
00:10:49,540 --> 00:10:51,540
Those machines…

215
00:10:51,540 --> 00:11:00,540
Your family's company makes the DES machines that attack our concerts.

216
00:11:00,540 --> 00:11:01,540
It's suspicious.

217
00:11:01,540 --> 00:11:02,540
Really suspicious.

218
00:11:02,540 --> 00:11:03,540
Chiri, are you a DES spy?

219
00:11:03,540 --> 00:11:04,540
That's harsh!

220
00:11:04,540 --> 00:11:05,540
How could you choose her of that?

221
00:11:05,540 --> 00:11:06,540
How could I not?

222
00:11:06,540 --> 00:11:07,540
Are you kind?

223
00:11:07,540 --> 00:11:08,540
Look, it's obvious.

224
00:11:08,540 --> 00:11:09,540
Senpai!

225
00:11:09,540 --> 00:11:10,540
What?

226
00:11:10,540 --> 00:11:11,540
What's going on?

227
00:11:11,540 --> 00:11:12,540
Take a look at this article.

228
00:11:14,540 --> 00:11:15,540
Chiri…

229
00:11:17,540 --> 00:11:18,540
Wait!

230
00:11:18,540 --> 00:11:19,540
Ever since…

231
00:11:19,540 --> 00:11:37,540
Ever since we saw that concert together, I've wanted to join Zero Zero.

232
00:11:37,540 --> 00:11:43,540
But no matter how many times I told my father I wanted to audition, he wouldn't let me.

233
00:11:43,540 --> 00:11:50,540
But I just couldn't give it up.

234
00:11:50,540 --> 00:11:54,540
I secretly went to a Zero Zero concert one more time.

235
00:11:54,540 --> 00:11:56,540
There was a DES attack.

236
00:11:56,540 --> 00:12:03,540
The machines used by the DES in the attack were made by my father's company.

237
00:12:03,540 --> 00:12:08,540
That's why I ran away from home when I found out about the audition here.

238
00:12:08,540 --> 00:12:17,540
From everyone else's point of view, I'm the unforgivable daughter of their unforgivable enemy.

239
00:12:17,540 --> 00:12:21,540
But I had to come, even though I knew I didn't belong here.

240
00:12:21,540 --> 00:12:22,540
That's not true!

241
00:12:22,540 --> 00:12:26,540
I want to become a successor with you and stand on this stage together!

242
00:12:26,540 --> 00:12:27,540
I'm sorry.

243
00:12:27,540 --> 00:12:30,540
Will you leave me alone for a while?

244
00:12:38,540 --> 00:12:44,540
Standing in the line right now, you can proceed right.

245
00:12:44,540 --> 00:12:46,540
All eyes are on.

246
00:12:46,540 --> 00:12:47,540
That's impressive!

247
00:12:47,540 --> 00:12:49,540
All these AKP songs!

248
00:12:49,540 --> 00:12:52,540
It's fun to practice singing like this once in a while.

249
00:12:52,540 --> 00:12:53,540
It's not practice!

250
00:12:53,540 --> 00:12:54,540
It's just karaoke!

251
00:12:54,540 --> 00:12:55,540
And I know…

252
00:12:55,540 --> 00:12:58,540
Doing this won't help us become successors.

253
00:12:58,540 --> 00:13:01,540
I actually think practicing will get us there sooner.

254
00:13:01,540 --> 00:13:03,540
But I'm dead fast and I'm drunk.

255
00:13:03,540 --> 00:13:04,540
And I'm drunk from here.

256
00:13:04,540 --> 00:13:05,540
I will not be too long.

257
00:13:05,540 --> 00:13:08,540
Still I'm the only one!

258
00:13:08,540 --> 00:13:10,540
Into me standing!

259
00:13:10,540 --> 00:13:12,540
It's not karaoke!

260
00:13:12,540 --> 00:13:14,540
It's in Kenya!

261
00:13:14,540 --> 00:13:17,540
Okay, good work!

262
00:13:17,540 --> 00:13:19,540
The successors can leave.

263
00:13:19,540 --> 00:13:21,540
I want the trainee understudies to stay here.

264
00:13:21,540 --> 00:13:22,540
Thank you very much!

265
00:13:22,540 --> 00:13:24,540
Chieri didn't know.

266
00:13:24,540 --> 00:13:27,540
Yeah, I wonder what happened.

267
00:13:27,540 --> 00:13:29,540
Ushiyama Sensei…

268
00:13:29,540 --> 00:13:32,540
Excuse me, I'm going to go get Chieri.

269
00:13:32,540 --> 00:13:34,540
Stop!

270
00:13:34,540 --> 00:13:35,540
What?

271
00:13:35,540 --> 00:13:38,540
I understand that you're concerned about your fellow trainee.

272
00:13:38,540 --> 00:13:39,540
That's to be commended.

273
00:13:39,540 --> 00:13:41,540
But right now, you have a role as an understudy,

274
00:13:41,540 --> 00:13:43,540
so you're staying here.

275
00:13:43,540 --> 00:13:45,540
A role, huh?

276
00:13:45,540 --> 00:13:47,540
Chieri abandoned that role.

277
00:13:47,540 --> 00:13:50,540
You don't have the time to worry about her.

278
00:13:50,540 --> 00:13:54,540
